      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b768d00ac2911529d5488cb|full_name}: The parameter \"Real User Height\" is generally very strange. It does not change the size of the avatar, but simply shifts the position of the avatar's view ball relative to the 3D-model. As a result, the avatar either crouches or tiptoes. Moreover, for each avatar, this shift is different and varies within very wide limits. I think that every avatar should have a checkbox \"Match the Real User Height\". If the checkbox is enabled, the size of the avatar must match the actual height of the user. If a player uses a small avatar and does not want to change its size, then he disables the checkbox.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-05T03:39:03.564Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In desktop mode when we lower our head down, the avatar straightens its legs and stands on tiptoe. When we raise our head up, the avatar bends the legs at the knees. This happens absolutely on all avatars. Someone more, someone less.",
